      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This problem needs a solution, otherwise I will be stuck using outdated packages to create worlds. I have only been able to use a legacy package 3.0 to create worlds and if support is withdrawn for 3.0, I will no longer be able to upload worlds. I hated the Creator Companion since day 1 and refused to use it, and now this problem makes me hate it even more. I wish they'd delete it and go back to manually installed packages. At least that was reliable and always worked. It was also faster because you only had to download one thing and drop it in the Unity project. Now you have to download 3 things and hope the stupid program will figure itself out, which in my case it doesn't. Why the f*** did they have to ditch the reliable and simpler method? The CC is an absurd and unnecessary \"solution\" to a nonexistent problem. And now y'all are using it and accepting it even though it was stupid and unnecessary to begin with.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
