      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "When I selected the avatar package, it had no issues downloading the 3.4.0 version right away. It was only the Worlds 3.4.0 that it failed to download. \n\nHOWEVER, I have thought of a solution, which so far seems like it might be working. I am downloading each worlds package version in chronological order, and it hasn't failed yet. I haven't made it to 3.4.0 yet, but so far it seems like this is working.\n\nEven if this works, this is still really stupid and it shouldn't have to be done this way. If it can download the Avatars 3.4.0 package without needing the previous versions first, then it shouldn't have any issue with getting the Worlds 3.4.0. It is absurd that I have to manually select each version in chronological order to get up to 3.4.0. If the developers of CC ignore this they're fools.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
